WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.284
If you may need nursing home care,

2
00:00:04.284 --> 00:00:10.100
Medicaid looks back five years at your gifts.

3
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.364
Medicare doesn't pay for long-term care.

4
00:00:14.364 --> 00:00:19.265
Medicaid does, but only when your assets and income

5
00:00:19.265 --> 00:00:21.100
are low.

6
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:26.945
If you gave away assets in that window before applying,

7
00:00:26.945 --> 00:00:33.100
Medicaid can set a penalty period when it won't pay.

8
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.301
Gifts to family,

9
00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.338
retitling a home,

10
00:00:37.338 --> 00:00:42.100
even large cash transfers may count.

11
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.480
There are exceptions,

12
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.127
for example for a spouse or a disabled child.

13
00:00:49.127 --> 00:00:53.600
They are technical and vary by state.

14
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:59.024
Planning early gives more choices than planning

15
00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:01.600
in a crisis.

16
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.725
Don't move assets before talking to an elder

17
00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:08.503
law attorney in your state.

18
00:01:08.503 --> 00:01:12.100
Our guide explains the basics.
